menu "Storage"

choice STORAGE_BACKEND
    prompt "Storage backend"
    default STORAGE_BACKEND_NVS
    help
        Selects the persistence backend behind the key_store / intent_log
        seam. The Application Module talks ONLY to the interfaces in
        key_store.h and intent_log.h — swapping the backend must never change
        an application call site.

        NVS is the default: keys and intent targets survive power loss via
        the ESP32's SPI flash partition.

        The Secure Element backend is planned and is an honest stub until the
        hardware lands.

    config STORAGE_BACKEND_NVS
        bool "NVS flash backend"

    config STORAGE_BACKEND_SE
        bool "Secure Element backend (stub)"
        help
            Honest stub — every call logs TODO(hardware) and returns an error.
            Implement the real driver behind the same storage_hal.h interface
            when the hardware lands.

endchoice

endmenu
